 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "globe",
   "text": "How did Spain go from a new republic to civil war in five years?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "It voted out its king in 1931. By 1936, the country was split down the middle."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "How did the king go?",
   "scene": "alfonso",
   "date": "14 April 1931",
   "place": "Madrid",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.33,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "In April 1931, republicans swept the city elections, and King Alfonso the Thirteenth left Spain. A republic was born."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "What did it change?",
   "scene": "start",
   "date": "1931",
   "place": "Spain"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "It moved fast: land reform, army reform, church and state split. In 1933, women voted for the first time."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "But Spain was divided. In 1934, miners in Asturias rose in revolt.",
   "scene": "asturias",
   "date": "October 1934",
   "place": "Asturias",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "The army crushed them, with a general named Francisco Franco directing from Madrid.",
   "scene": "arrests",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And then?",
   "scene": "poster",
   "date": "February 1936",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "In 1936, the left-wing Popular Front won the election. Strikes, church burnings and political killings followed, on both sides."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "In July, police officers murdered the right-wing leader José Calvo Sotelo."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So the army moved?",
   "scene": "coup",
   "date": "18 July 1936",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Days later, generals rose against the Republic. The coup won in about half of Spain, and failed in the rest."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "What did the map look like?",
   "scene": "end",
   "date": "July 1936",
   "place": "Spain"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Two Spains. The rebels held the northwest and pockets of the south. The Republic held Madrid, Barcelona and the east."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Franco's best troops were stuck in Morocco. Hitler and Mussolini sent planes, and flew them across. By October, Franco led the rebels.",
   "scene": "franco",
   "date": "1 October 1936",
   "place": "Burgos",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Next time: three years of civil war. Like the video and follow History Sketches."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And tell us in the comments what you think!"
  },
  {
   "type": "end",
   "text": "Next: three years of civil war",
   "sub": "Follow History Sketches"
  }
 ],
